## DESCRIPTION
## Proof of Taylor’s theorem
## ENDDESCRIPTION

## DBsubject('Calculus - multivariable')
## DBchapter('Differentiation of multivariable functions')
## DBsection('Proof of Taylor’s theorem')

DOCUMENT();

loadMacros("PGstandard.pl", "PGchoicemacros.pl");

TEXT(beginproblem());

$mc = new_checkbox_multiple_choice();
$mc -> qa(
"Let \( f: \mathbb{R}^n \to \mathbb{R} \) be a function. Let \( a \in \mathbb{R}^n \) and \( N \in \mathbb{N}^+ \). If it exists, let \( P_N \) be the \( N \)th Taylor polynomial of \( f \) at \( a \) and let \( R_N \) be the \( N \)th remainder of \( f \) at \( a \). Which of the following are true?",
"Fix \( i \in \{1,\dots,n\} \). If \( f \) is \( C^k \) then \( \dfrac{\partial f}{\partial x_i} \) is \( C^{k-1} \).",
"Fix \( h \in \mathbb{R}^n \). If \( f \) is \( C^N \) then \( D_hf \) is \( C^{N-1} \).",
"Fix \( h \in \mathbb{R}^n \) and \( k \in \{1,\dots,N\} \). If \( f \) is \( C^N \) then \( D_h^kf \) is \( C^{N-k} \).",
"If \( f: \mathbb{R}^n \to \mathbb{R} \) is \( C^1 \) and \( \varphi: \mathbb{R} \to \mathbb{R}^n \) is \( C^1 \) then \( f \circ \varphi: \mathbb{R} \to \mathbb{R} \) is \( C^1 \).",
"If \( f \) is \( C^{N+1} \) on an open ball of \( a \) then \( \lim_{x \to a} \dfrac{R_N(x)}{||x-a||^N} = 0 \).",
"If \( Q \) is a polynomial in \( n \) variables of degree \( \leq N \) such that \( \lim_{x \to 0} \dfrac{Q(x)}{||x||^N}=0 \), then \( Q \) is the zero polynomial."
);

$mc -> makeLast(
"Fix \( i \in \{1,\dots,n\} \). If \( f \) is \( C^k \) then \( \dfrac{\partial f}{\partial x_i} \) is \( C^{k-1} \).",
"Fix \( h \in \mathbb{R}^n \). If \( f \) is \( C^N \) then \( D_hf \) is \( C^{N-1} \).",
"Fix \( h \in \mathbb{R}^n \) and \( k \in \{1,\dots,N\} \). If \( f \) is \( C^N \) then \( D_h^kf \) is \( C^{N-k} \).",
"If \( f: \mathbb{R}^n \to \mathbb{R} \) is \( C^1 \) and \( \varphi: \mathbb{R} \to \mathbb{R}^n \) is \( C^1 \) then \( f \circ \varphi: \mathbb{R} \to \mathbb{R} \) is \( C^1 \).",
"If \( f \) is \( C^{N+1} \) on an open ball of \( a \) then \( \lim_{x \to a} \dfrac{R_N(x)}{||x-a||^N} = 0 \).",
"If \( Q \) is a polynomial in \( n \) variables of degree \( \leq N \) such that \( \lim_{x \to 0} \dfrac{Q(x)}{||x||^N}=0 \), then \( Q \) is the zero polynomial."
);

BEGIN_TEXT
$BR
\{ $mc->print_q() \}
$BR
\{ $mc->print_a() \}
END_TEXT

$showPartialCorrectAnswers = 0;
ANS( checkbox_cmp( $mc->correct_ans() ) );

BEGIN_SOLUTION
All of them are true. C can be proved by induction. E is Taylor’s theorem. F is Lemma 6.6.8.
END_SOLUTION

ENDDOCUMENT();